<%# NO .page wrapper of its own, deliberately -- same reason as
    withdrawn.html.erb, which this view is modelled on: halt_if_pass_revoked
    renders this under the APPLICATION layout, which has already opened
    <div class="page">, and .page carries min-height: 100svh, so a second one
    nested inside it stacks a full viewport below the sticky topbar. Measured
    at 390x680, 375x553 and 1280x800 with the wrapper: 849/722/917px document,
    169/169/117px of dead scroll. Without it: 680/553/800px, exactly one
    viewport. Neither suite can see this -- Capybara parses no CSS, and
    bin/measure-play-screen measures the play screen, not this one. %>
<h2><%= t("errors.access_revoked") %></h2>
<p><%= t("game_passings.pass_revoked.what_to_do") %></p>
<p><%= link_to @game.name, game_path(@game) %></p>
